  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A spherical mirror is obtained as shown in the figure from a hollow glass sphere, if an object is positioned in front&nbsp;of the mirror, what will be the nature and magnification of the image of the object? (Figure down&nbsp;as schematic and not to scale)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0187_b2278a8e1133.png\" style=\"width: 307px; height: 185px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Inverted, real and magnified",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Erect, virtual and magnified",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Erect, virutual and unmagnified",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Inverted, real and unmagnified",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The image will form between&nbsp;the focus and centre&nbsp;of&nbsp;the concave mirror when we keep the object between the&nbsp;centre and infinity.It will be real image.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0187_8b76b374a534.png\" style=\"width: 312px; height: 236px;\" /></p>"
  }
}